AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000377 "A hardware channel type of acquisition_channels.channels.type; the NDI v1 channel prefix is 'mk' (a code, not a synonym) (the migrator maps prefix to term, NDI maps term to prefix for its readers). Under NCIT Channel (C44170), the root of the channel-type binding, whose other two values are NCIT Metadata (C52095, v1 md) and NCIT Text (C25704, v1 tx). The 8 derived read modes (dep den dimp dimn aep aen aimp aimn) get no terms. No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-22, label and synonym search; queries analog input, analog input channel, analog output, digital input, digital output, auxiliary input, time channel, event channel, marker channel, trigger channel, event marker: 0 hits each). Source: Jess Haley, 2026-10-22, did-schema tenet audit [B2 channel types].")
