# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000383 (recording epoch)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000383 "One continuous stretch of recording, whose files may be written by one or more acquisition systems.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000383 "The node of the did-schema entity type epoch. No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-22; queries recording epoch, epoch, recording period, time period): NCIT Clinical Trial Epoch (C71738) and Baseline Epoch (C125938) are trial phases; OM epoch is a unit. Under NCIT Period (C25616, an interval of time), as the entity type session is NCIT Session (C67447). Source: Jess Haley, 2026-10-22, did-schema tenet audit [L3].")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000383 "recording epoch"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000383 obo:NCIT_C25616)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000384 (signed distance to region boundary)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000384 "The distance from a point to the nearest boundary of a region, positive inside the region and negative outside it.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000384 "Replaces EMPTY:0000350 (signed distance from the nearest bacterial patch edge): the region is named by a condition that points at the region's mask. As distanceLawnEdge in analyzeWormLabTracks (Haley et al. 2024), the signed distance transform of a mask read at a point. Under PATO distance, as EMPTY:0000350 was. No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-22; query signed distance: 1 hit, MeSH Phylogeny, unrelated). Source: Jess Haley, 2026-10-22, did-schema tenet audit [O3 Haley terms general].")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000384 "signed distance to region boundary"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000384 obo:PATO_0000040)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000385 (seeding volume)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000385 "The volume of a solution or suspension placed to seed a culture.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000385 "Replaces EMPTY:0000120 (bacterial patch volume): what was seeded and where is said by the document. Under parameter and NCIT Volume (C25335), as EMPTY:0000120 was under bacterial parameter and NCIT Volume. No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-22; queries seeding volume, inoculum volume, inoculation volume): TO seed volume (0007000) is the volume of a plant seed; the other two have 0 hits. Source: Jess Haley, 2026-10-22, did-schema tenet audit [O3 Haley terms general].")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000385 "seeding volume"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000385 obo:EMPTY_0000080)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000385 obo:NCIT_C25335)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000387 (Chebyshev type I filter)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000387 "A filter design with equal ripple in the passband and a monotonic stopband, giving a steeper transition than a Butterworth design of the same order.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000387 "No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-22; queries Chebyshev filter, Chebyshev type I filter, digital filter, signal filtering): no OBO ontology has signal-filter designs; OBI band-pass, long-pass and short-pass filters are optical filters. Wikidata Chebyshev filter (Q718621) names both types together, so it is a cross-reference, not this term's node. Written by DID-matlab jFrequencyFilter, the migrator of v1 filter documents. Under data transformation (OBI:0200000): a filter applied to a signal is a method [filters are methods]. Source: did-schema V_eta_frequency_filter_model_plan.md [filter terms from Wikidata]. Jess Haley, 2026-10-22.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000387 "Chebyshev type I filter"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000387 obo:OBI_0200000)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000388 (Chebyshev type II filter)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000388 "A filter design with a monotonic passband and equal ripple in the stopband.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000388 "No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-22; queries as for EMPTY:0000387, plus inverse Chebyshev filter). Wikidata Chebyshev filter (Q718621) names both types together. Written by DID-matlab jFrequencyFilter. Under data transformation (OBI:0200000). Source: did-schema V_eta_frequency_filter_model_plan.md [filter terms from Wikidata]. Jess Haley, 2026-10-22.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000388 "Chebyshev type II filter"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:EMPTY_0000388 "inverse Chebyshev filter"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000388 obo:OBI_0200000)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000389 (filter band)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000389 "Which range of frequencies a filter passes and which it attenuates.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000389 "The variable whose values are high-pass, low-pass, band-pass and band-stop filter (Wikidata Q262754, Q918242, Q2718101, Q386022). No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-22; queries filter band, filter type, filter response type): NCIT Reconstruction Filter Type (C106564) is about image reconstruction. Under parameter. Source: did-schema V_eta_frequency_filter_model_plan.md [filter terms from Wikidata]. Jess Haley, 2026-10-22.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000389 "filter band"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000389 obo:EMPTY_0000080)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000390 (passband low edge)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000390 "The lowest frequency a filter is designed to pass.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000390 "Paired with passband high edge (EMPTY:0000391). No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-22; queries passband edge, passband, cutoff frequency): NCIT Filter Cutoff Frequency (C94895) names an upper cutoff only. Under parameter. Source: did-schema V_eta_frequency_filter_model_plan.md [passband edges paired]. Jess Haley, 2026-10-22.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000390 "passband low edge"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:EMPTY_0000390 "low cutoff frequency"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000390 obo:EMPTY_0000080)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000391 (passband high edge)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000391 "The highest frequency a filter is designed to pass.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000391 "Paired with passband low edge (EMPTY:0000390). NCIT Filter Cutoff Frequency (C94895), the upper limit for the frequency content that essentially passes through a filter, is close but names the cutoff, often the -3 dB point, not the design edge, and has no lower counterpart; it is a cross-reference, not this term's node. Under parameter. Source: did-schema V_eta_frequency_filter_model_plan.md [passband edges paired]. Jess Haley, 2026-10-22.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000391 "passband high edge"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:EMPTY_0000391 "high cutoff frequency"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000391 obo:EMPTY_0000080)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000392 (stopband low edge)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000392 "The lowest frequency of the range a filter is designed to attenuate.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000392 "No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-22; queries stopband, stopband edge): Wikidata stopband (Q1971063) names the band, not an edge. Under parameter. Source: did-schema V_eta_frequency_filter_model_plan.md [filter terms from Wikidata]. Jess Haley, 2026-10-22.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000392 "stopband low edge"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000392 obo:EMPTY_0000080)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000393 (stopband high edge)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000393 "The highest frequency of the range a filter is designed to attenuate.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000393 "No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-22; queries as for EMPTY:0000392). Under parameter. Source: did-schema V_eta_frequency_filter_model_plan.md [filter terms from Wikidata]. Jess Haley, 2026-10-22.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000393 "stopband high edge"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000393 obo:EMPTY_0000080)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000394 (filter order)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000394 "The order of a filter's transfer function, which sets how steeply the filter changes from passing to attenuating.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000394 "No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-22; queries filter order, order of filter). Under parameter. Source: did-schema V_eta_frequency_filter_model_plan.md [filter terms from Wikidata]. Jess Haley, 2026-10-22.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000394 "filter order"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000394 obo:EMPTY_0000080)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000395 (passband ripple)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000395 "The peak-to-peak variation of a filter's gain within its passband.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000395 "No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-22; queries passband ripple, ripple): Wikidata ripple (Q1776117) is power-supply ripple. Under parameter. Source: did-schema V_eta_frequency_filter_model_plan.md [filter terms from Wikidata]. Jess Haley, 2026-10-22.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000395 "passband ripple"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000395 obo:EMPTY_0000080)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000396 (stopband attenuation)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000396 "The minimum reduction of a filter's gain in its stopband relative to its passband.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000396 "No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-22; queries stopband attenuation, attenuation). Under parameter. Source: did-schema V_eta_frequency_filter_model_plan.md [filter terms from Wikidata]. Jess Haley, 2026-10-22.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000396 "stopband attenuation"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000396 obo:EMPTY_0000080)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000397 (dF/F)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000397 "The change in fluorescence relative to a baseline fluorescence, (F - F0)/F0.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000397 "The quantity a calcium-imaging or other fluorescence response is measured in; its unit is om:one. No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-22; queries dF/F, delta F/F, fluorescence change, relative fluorescence: UO relative fluorescence unit (0000314) and NCIT Relative Fluorescence Intensity Unit (C77535) are units, not this quantity; Wikidata, 2026-10-22, exact labels dF/F, delta F/F, relative fluorescence change, fractional fluorescence change: none). Under PATO ratio (PATO:0001470). Source: did-schema V_eta_data_body_model_plan.md [dF/F as variable] and [response variable nodes]. Jess Haley, 2026-10-22.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000397 "dF/F"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:EMPTY_0000397 "ΔF/F"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000397 obo:PATO_0001470)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000398 (neural response)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000398 "The activity of a neuron or population of neurons measured in response to a stimulus.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000398 "The general variable of a tuning or other stimulus-response calculation whose source does not state the quantity measured (a firing rate is wikidata:Q71762818, dF/F is EMPTY:0000397). No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-23; exact queries neural response: 0 hits; neuronal response, stimulus response, neural activity: only diseases, genes, assays, cell types and GO response processes, none the measured quantity). Under PATO quality (PATO:0000001). Source: did-schema V_eta_data_body_model_plan.md [unstated response variable]. Jess Haley, 2026-10-23.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000398 "neural response"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000398 obo:PATO_0000001)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000399 (database ingestion)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000399 "A process in which the records held in one database are copied into another database, which thereafter holds them itself.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000399 "The method of a session's membership in a dataset when the session's records were ingested (NDI v1 session_in_a_dataset is_linked = 0; ndi.dataset add_ingested_session). No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-26; queries data ingestion, ingest, data import, data import process, database import, data copying, data transfer): T4FS data ingestion (0000290) also includes processing and reformatting data, and its prefix is not in the NDI term registry; MI imported (1058) is a curation status. Under NCIT Data Processing (C47925). Source: did-schema V_eta_go_forward_class_audit.md [census terms] T1 and [session membership records linked or ingested]. Jess Haley, 2026-10-26.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000399 "database ingestion"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000399 obo:NCIT_C47925)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000400 (database linking)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000400 "A process in which one database records a reference to another database stored elsewhere, whose records stay where they are and are read from there.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000400 "The method of a session's membership in a dataset when the session was linked (NDI v1 session_in_a_dataset is_linked = 1; ndi.dataset add_linked_session). No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-26; queries linked data, data linking, database link, database federation, data virtualization, pointer, hyperlink, external data reference): T4FS data linkage (0000423) and NCIT Record Linkage Study (C15424) mean linking records of the same individual; NCIT Pointer (C48909) is an address, not a process. Under NCIT Data Processing (C47925). Source: did-schema V_eta_go_forward_class_audit.md [census terms] T1 and [session membership records linked or ingested]. Jess Haley, 2026-10-26.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000400 "database linking"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000400 obo:NCIT_C47925)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000401 (software class)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000401 "A class defined in a software library, named by its fully qualified name, whose constructor creates an object from a list of arguments.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000401 "The variable of a linked session's opener class (NDI v1 session_in_a_dataset session_creator, for example ndi.session.dir), a parameter of the database linking method. No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-26; queries class name, constructor, object class, class in SWO): NCIT Object Class (C41106) is an ISO 11179 data-modelling notion and IAO named class expression (0000421) is an OWL expression; neither names a class in code. Under IAO information content entity (IAO:0000030). Source: did-schema V_eta_go_forward_class_audit.md [census terms] T1. Jess Haley, 2026-10-26.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000401 "software class"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000401 obo:IAO_0000030)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000402 (value range)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000402 "The lowest and highest values that the values of a data body may take, given as a pair [minimum maximum].")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000402 "Written as a condition on an image data body only when NDI v1 image or imageStack data_limits differs from the range of its data type. NCIT Range (C38013) leads with a single difference ('The difference between the lowest and highest numerical values'), not the pair. Other OLS4 results (2026-10-26; queries value range, data range, range of values, dynamic range, minimum and maximum value, intensity range, pixel value range): STATO range (0000035) is a scalar measure of variation; NCIT Dynamic Range (C94889) is a difference or ratio; NCIT Reference Range (C71474) is for clinical results. Under IAO data item (IAO:0000027). Source: did-schema V_eta_go_forward_class_audit.md [census terms] T3 and [image file details placed]. Jess Haley, 2026-10-26.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000402 "value range"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000402 obo:IAO_0000027)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000403 (device local time)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000403 "A time scale kept by a recording device that runs only within one recording epoch, so that times on it cannot be compared across epochs.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000403 "A clock of a relative time reference; the NDI v1 clock type code is 'dev_local_time' (a code, not a synonym), defined in NDI ndi.time.clocktype as 'A device keeps its own local time only within epochs'. No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-26; queries clock time, device clock, local time, system clock, global time, time scale): NCIT Clock Device Time (C207913) does not separate local, device-global and experiment-global time. Under NCIT Clock Device Time (C207913). Source: did-schema V_eta_go_forward_class_audit.md [census terms] T4 and [clock terms get nodes]. Jess Haley, 2026-10-26.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000403 "device local time"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000403 obo:NCIT_C207913)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000404 (device global time)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000404 "A time scale kept by a recording device that runs continuously across its recording epochs, so that times on it can be compared across those epochs of that device.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000404 "A clock of a relative time reference; the NDI v1 clock type code is 'dev_global_time' (a code, not a synonym), defined in NDI ndi.time.clocktype as a device that 'keeps its own global time ... (that is, it knows its own clock across recording epochs)'. No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-26; queries clock time, device clock, local time, system clock, global time, time scale): NCIT Clock Device Time (C207913) does not separate local, device-global and experiment-global time. Under NCIT Clock Device Time (C207913). Source: did-schema V_eta_go_forward_class_audit.md [census terms] T4 and [clock terms get nodes]. Jess Haley, 2026-10-26.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000404 "device global time"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000404 obo:NCIT_C207913)

# Class: obo:EMPTY_0000405 (experiment global time)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:EMPTY_0000405 "A time scale shared by all the devices of an experiment, to which their own clocks are aligned, so that times from different devices can be compared.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:EMPTY_0000405 "A clock of a relative time reference; the NDI v1 clock type code is 'exp_global_time' (a code, not a synonym), defined in NDI ndi.time.clocktype as 'Experiment global time (within 0.1ms)'. No ontology term found (OLS4, 2026-10-26; queries clock time, device clock, local time, system clock, global time, time scale): NCIT Clock Device Time (C207913) does not separate local, device-global and experiment-global time; the fourth clock, utc, is Wikidata Coordinated Universal Time (Q1536). Under NCIT Clock Device Time (C207913). Source: did-schema V_eta_go_forward_class_audit.md [census terms] T4 and [clock terms get nodes]. Jess Haley, 2026-10-26.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:EMPTY_0000405 "experiment global time"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:EMPTY_0000405 obo:NCIT_C207913)

